# docs/ never gets committed. This repo is public (or about to be), and the
# notes in there describe my own infrastructure and where it's weak -- that is
# not something to publish next to my CV.
#
# Keep it that way. If I ever need one of those files on another machine, copy
# it across by hand rather than "just this once" committing it.
#
# _config.yml also excludes docs/ from the Jekyll build, which is the belt to
# this braces: if a file ever does slip into a commit, it still won't be served.
docs/

# scratch files from poking at the site
audit.json
*.log

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
